  "id": "weapon-focus-effect",
  "term": "weapon-focus effect",
  "definition": "The weapon-focus effect is the finding that a person seen in a scene with a gun is remembered less accurately. It is understood as attention being drawn to the weapon because it is unusual or threatening, which reduces encoding of other parts of the scene.",
